{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"floating-guiltless-oxpecker","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py` (from golden-busied-nag, `d5f10d1d2c8`) hard-codes the reviewed base as `BASE_REMOTE = \"origin\"` / `BASE_REF = \"refs/remotes/origin/main\"`. In a repository whose integration branch is not `main` (for example `master` or `trunk`), or whose remote is not named `origin`, `base_ref()` finds no such ref and `rebar verify-opcert` exits 2 with a misleading \"fetch origin main\" hint. Rebar is used in other repositories, so the gate is unusable there. The rest of rebar names its sync remote with `sync.remote` (`src/rebar/_config_schema.py`, `SyncConfig.remote`, default `origin`) and its gate base ref with `REBAR_GATE_REF` > `[snapshot].ref` > `origin/main` (`rebar.llm.gate_source.default_ref`, `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py` `resolve_gate_ref`). No config key, env var or flag may be added.\n\nThe constraint that shapes the fix: the base ref decides which `rebar.toml` the gate trusts, so it must not come from the change under review. A working-tree `[snapshot].ref` or `sync.remote` could point the gate at the change's own branch.\n\n## Approach\n\nResolve the base in `base_ref()` from sources the change under review cannot edit, in this order:\n1. `REBAR_GATE_REF`, the existing environment override, read through `rebar.config.resolve_gate_ref` semantics but from the environment only (a CI job sets it for a non-`main` repo).\n2. The remote's recorded default branch, `refs/remotes/<remote>/HEAD` (git sets it on clone, or `git remote set-head <remote> --auto`).\n3. `refs/remotes/<remote>/main`, today's behaviour.\n`<remote>` is `sync.remote` taken from the user and environment layers only (`REBAR_SYNC_REMOTE`, user `config.toml`), defaulting to `origin`; never from a working-tree config.\n\nThen honour the repository's own reviewed setting: after reading the committed project config at that base, if it sets `[snapshot].ref` (or `[sync].remote`) to a different branch, re-resolve once to that ref and read the committed config there. That value is itself reviewed (it is committed on the base), so a repository whose rebar.toml says `[snapshot] ref = \"origin/master\"` gates against master. One hop only, so a committed config cannot chain.\n\nThe not-found error names the remote and branch actually tried and the `git fetch` that fixes it. `.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` is unchanged (this repository's base is `main`).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt`, `docs/cli-reference.md` (describe the base resolution)\n\n## Testing\n\nIn `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`, with local bare repos:\n- A repository whose only branch is `master`, cloned so `origin/HEAD` points at `origin/master`: the gate reads `origin/master:rebar.toml` and exits by main-equivalent rules, not 2.\n- A remote named `upstream` with `REBAR_SYNC_REMOTE=upstream`: the gate reads `upstream`'s default branch.\n- `REBAR_GATE_REF=refs/remotes/origin/trunk` set: that ref wins.\n- A working-tree `rebar.toml` that sets `[snapshot] ref` or `[sync] remote` to the change's branch is ignored.\n- The committed config on main sets `[snapshot] ref = \"origin/release\"`: the gate re-resolves once to `origin/release`; a second-level ref in release's config is not followed.\n- No resolvable base: exit 2 naming the remote and branch tried.\nExisting gate tests pass unchanged. Then `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] On a repository whose default branch is `master`, `rebar verify-opcert` reads the committed config from `origin/master` and does not exit 2: shown by a test in `tests/unit/test_opcert_gate_config.py`.\n- [ ] `REBAR_GATE_REF` and the environment's `sync.remote` select the base, and a working-tree `[snapshot].ref` or `[sync].remote` does not: shown by tests.\n- [ ] A committed `[snapshot].ref` on the base is followed once and only once: shown by a test.\n- [ ] With no resolvable base the exit is 2 and the message names the remote and branch tried.\n- [ ] No config key, env var or flag is added: `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 and `git diff origin/main -- src/rebar/_config_schema.py` is empty.","id":"35eb-bf90-0c47-4b64","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"verify-opcert hard-codes origin/main as the reviewed base"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795245184374679001,"uuid":"41e49dab-52a1-4a63-9031-b1a57f3ea1d5"}